      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a decent start, but I'm looking at the dashboard and the \"thoroughness\" score for this draft is actually quite low compared to some of the other reviews in the queue. \n\nThe ranking algorithm seems to be heavily weighing the structural organization/granularity. The top-rated reviews aren't necessarily longer, but they seem to have a much more detailed organizational breakdown. It's not about fluff, but about making every specific critique very clearly delineated so they don't get lost.\n\nCould you refine this? Try to be more granular with the critique—especially on the methodology and the precursor temperature issues—and use a more robust organizational structure so the automated tool picks up on the depth of the analysis. Again, just make sure it stays professional.",
